{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503319-the-exarchs-and-the-aeons","id":1503319,"title":"The Exarchs and the Aeons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-02-17T08:33:34-08:00","id":1503319,"title":"The Exarchs and the Aeons","content":"How do y'all imagine or understand the interaction between the Exarchs and the Aeons? Do they ever interact (I imagine they must)? Are they enemies, rivals, lovers, opponents, friends, coworkers, tools of the other (or the Other), something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>either e/em/eir pronouns OR fey/fem/fear OR be/bim/bos pronouns {if you don't want to learn new words, singular they is OK}<br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/queermythopoeia\" target=\"_blank\">Support my RPG writing and streaming on Patreon</a>!<br /> <a href=\"https://luciferssubcreations.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Shards: Sub-Creations Taking Root in Ein Soph Aur</a> {an rpg blog}","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26484-tristissima-et-alia","name":"Tristissima et alia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T09:42:36-08:00","id":1503325,"title":"","content":"The Aeons are the way the human mind perceives the Arcana. When a being Ascends, the archetype they added to the Supernal may reshape how the Arcanum is perceived, like when Merlin creating the archetype of the Fisher King, it transformed the Aeon of Fate into Mordred.<br /> <br /> Because of that, in general I see the Aeons as neutral to the Exarchs and other major powers. Dahak is human evil, so he may be interested in evil acts that benefit himself or his agenda. But it won't make him instantly welcoming to an ochema or a presumed ally.<br /> <br /> There is one notable exception though, Typhon hates the Spire Perilous, so he may be persuaded to lend aid at the cost of destroying Awakened knowledge, if for no other reason than pure spite. But otherwise mages would have a hard time entreating him and anyone else would be horrified being in the presence of one of the few beings in the cosmos that could make Zeus fear for his life.\u200b The Exarchs and any other Ascended beings probably could talk to him, but he would resent their very existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T10:25:04-08:00","id":1503328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503319-the-exarchs-and-the-aeons?p=1503325#post1503325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Aeons are the way the human mind perceives the Arcana. &lt;Snip&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>I was under the impression that the Aeons are part of the Anima Mundi, not the Temenos? So regardless of human mind, they would be a reflection of the World Soul's 'perception' of the Arcana...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T11:31:44-08:00","id":1503334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503319-the-exarchs-and-the-aeons?p=1503328#post1503328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was under the impression that the Aeons are part of the Anima Mundi, not the Temenos? So regardless of human mind, they would be a reflection of the World Soul's 'perception' of the Arcana...</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point, its probably the perception every being in the world has of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T12:18:43-08:00","id":1503337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503319-the-exarchs-and-the-aeons?p=1503334#post1503334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point, its probably the perception every being in the world has of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation is that the Arcana - with all their purviews - make up the actual reality of the World; which the World Soul itself is reflecting.<br /> <br /> Doesn't change what you said about changing the symbology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T18:43:07-08:00","id":1503417,"title":"","content":"Some things suggest that the exact nature of the Aeons is a bit ambiguous; they exist in the space of what Second Edition calls Goetia, if among the most powerful of them, but people like archmages might think they're something like minor Supernal gods trapped or duty-bound on this side of the Abyss or are otherwise informed by the Supernal in ways set apart from any other Goetia. Certainly the Auctoritas Arcanum might be regarded as a means to possess and impart Supernal power that seems to step a bit beyond the rules for how entities of the Astral Realms tend to work.<br /> <br /> I think the Aeons are best regarded as relatively neutral actors concerning the Lie, neither actively preserving it or specifically opposing it. Some aspects of what a given Aeon represents seem to be compatible with a given Iron Seal, some of them don't, some are entirely focused on their own particular qualities of the Arcana. I think this is best for the sake of letting the Aeons by approachable by mages regardless of faction, where the main thing the Aeon gets out of those exchanges serves their own agendas, proclivities, what they perceive as the wellbeing of the Arcanum itself.<br /> <br /> It would make sense to me that the Aeons occasionally host emissaries of the Exarchs in the form of enslaved Supernal entities or Ochemata, the same way such beings are supposed to commune on their behalf to many of the godlike entities of the Fallen World, but I'd say the Exarchs often take a more light touch with them. More bargaining from a position of great strength than merely demanding, treating with them the way a colonial official might approach a regional prince; it's more trouble than it's worth to disrespect them in their own domain, so better to acknowledge their sovereignty and show decorum to keep them feeling that their interests and yours align so they'll be more invested in using some of their resources to benefit your purposes.<br /> <br /> That might sometimes mean that a mage, whether Seer or Pentacle or otherwise, is paying for their boon from an Aeon with some action that ultimately benefits what an Exarch wanted (in ways hard for mortal minds to comprehend), but not categorically, and in more than enough cases where it was more what the Aeon wanted that had nothing to do with the Exarchs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T22:58:25-08:00","id":1503427,"title":"","content":"It honestly wouldn't be too big a stretch to make the Aeons some of the Bound - perhaps they're necessary anchors the Exarchs had to make/leave in place, if they wanted to keep the Fallen tethered enough to the Supernal that even Exarchical might isn't barred by the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T00:21:08-08:00","id":1503434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503319-the-exarchs-and-the-aeons?p=1503427#post1503427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It honestly wouldn't be too big a stretch to make the Aeons some of the Bound - perhaps they're necessary anchors the Exarchs had to make/leave in place, if they wanted to keep the Fallen tethered enough to the Supernal that even Exarchical might isn't barred by the Abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Bound, almost definitionly, require mana to sustain themselves, and lacking the normal flow of mana in the Supernal, are hungry for it and will eat your pattern.<br /> <br /> The Aeons, by contrast, are in their native realm. And are likely so powerful that they essentially have infinite essence (if a ghost gets essence whenever someone really thinks about them, when does a goetia of Mind get essence? Whenever the mental capacity of the Universe is expressed?).<br /> <br /> If they didn't exist, it would make sense for the Anima Mundi to create them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T06:25:23-08:00","id":1503444,"title":"","content":"Possibly being analogous to the Bound is something that could be an origin for the Aeons, although they're evidently not constrained by the same rules or have the same needs.<br /> <br /> I think this is one of those cases where it's better to look upon their ambiguities in terms of being a mystery that is the typical level on which one interacts with them, rather than something a person should feel the need to find answers for outside of the game for the sake of having ready answers for every scenario that might intersect with them. I think it mostly suffices to say that they're Goetia who, between being personifications of the Arcana and having Rank 8*, have a level of significance way beyond most other Goetia one could ever interact with in the setting.<br /> <br /> For the sake of the question that started the thread, I think the primary concern is that they need to be neutral enough in relation to the Exarchs that it's possible for mages from any sect to approach them. Signs of Sorcery makes it most clear that Mysteries directly related to the Exarchs are highly compromising to approach, so the Aeons cannot be that and still fulfil their intended narrative function.<br /> <br /> I think if one is looking to reconcile parts of the setting, it's most straightforward to say that the Exarchs sometimes entreat with the Aeons, but in most cases it's easy enough to do what they want without involving them at all. Whatever else the Aeons are, they don't seem to be integral to the actual functioning of the phenomena that fall under the Arcana within the world, and I think in most cases the kind of insight that people go to the Aeons looking for is already known to and exceeded by the Exarchs. That the Exarchs can't or won't enslave the Aeons can be the sort of Mystery that sends somebody on the path to Archmastery, whereas most mages are satisfied that the only peril in approaching them comes entirely from their own will.<br /> <br /> * Which I'll remind people is about as powerful as it's possible for an entity in the Fallen World to be without being basically theoretical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-19T06:42:47-08:00","id":1503445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1503319-the-exarchs-and-the-aeons?p=1503444#post1503444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever else the Aeons are, they don't seem to be integral to the actual functioning of the phenomena that fall under the Arcana within the world</div> </div> </div> </div>The same with the Temenos entities, it is not necessary for the functioning of human collective knowledge, but it is a reflection of it.<br /> <br /> Or like in evolution, they may be a spandrel, they don't need to have a purpose, the shape of the rest of the setting simply requires that they exist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}